//File:    contracts.jtext
//Date:    2026-10-29
//Purpose: The contract evaluation modes each toolchain can run, by OS (v002). jac313_test_cli
//         --contracts takes only a mode marked true here, and Jac313Runner enables only those.
//         enforce: a violation prints and ends the program (the default). observe: prints and
//         goes on. quick_enforce: ends it at once, without a message. ignore: not checked.
//         observe and quick_enforce need native C++26 contracts (GCC 16 at -std=c++26, so v002
//         only); elsewhere the JAC313_ / JTEXT_ / QLITE_ macros run (enforce) or are compiled
//         out (ignore). A toolchain with no row here has enforce and ignore.
//
=== jText File ===
 1. #?# contracts.jtext
 3. #?# Contract evaluation modes by OS and toolchain (v002)
 7. #?# contract_modes

